Cycles, amplitude, mean load and fatigue evidence (@mech-fatigue-history: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY", #source "../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W", #mechanical-engineering "../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/testing/Fatigue-cycles-crack-growth-and-variable-service.lingua#r_0TTB12YZSCY7ZNPB8G5CKS73Q5") { r_6JRBZ364N20J94XRYNVYFQ52MY
**Read:** [Modules in Mechanics of Materials — David Roylance](../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY), Fatigue; [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), section 9.2; then the shared metallurgy fatigue Record for mechanisms and experimental evidence.

A component can fail after many cycles below its monotonic yield strength. Define the local stress/strain history, mean, amplitude, range, stress ratio, sequence and failure criterion. A rotating shaft under a steady transverse load can experience alternating bending at a material point even though the external load is steady in the room frame.

For a stress cycling between 20 and 100 MPa, mean stress is 60 MPa, amplitude 40 MPa, range 80 MPa and R = σ_min/σ_max = 0.2. A fully reversed cycle has zero mean and R = −1 when the maximum is nonzero. Similar amplitudes at different means or environments need not give similar lives.

A reported runout means no specified failure was observed by the stopping cycle count; it is censored evidence, not a measured infinite life. A plateau in a particular S–N test series is not a universal guarantee against very-high-cycle or environmentally assisted damage. Frequency, heating and specimen effects must match the use of the data.

**Work:** Convert a machine's torque, bending and start/stop history into candidate local cycles. Separate simultaneous stress components and phase relationships. Read a complete documented fatigue study, including runouts and scatter, before applying a curve to a different surface, size, orientation or environment.

**Return:** [Mechanical engineering and machine design](../Mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design.lingua#r_0017YZ63HZBZ4P4WD8DECVWE4R).
